WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.220
Maybe they're a chore to sit through.

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:04.040
Perhaps they're just too disturbing.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:08.020
Or maybe they're so emotionally traumatic
that they left us weeping on the floor for

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:08.520
days.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.260
From melodramatic war movies to stunning but
slow-moving sci-fi, these are the greatest

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.000
movies we'll never watch again.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.500
War is hell, and while no film can truly capture
the horrors of battle, The Deer Hunter does

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:23.670
a pretty good job of taking moviegoers into
the ninth circle.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:28.890
This 1978 epic follows a trio of blue collar
steelworkers who can't wait to see action

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:29.640
in Vietnam.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.480
But when they finally descend into the jungle,
they're put through the worst tortures imaginable,

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.720
and the trauma doesn't stop once they come
back home.

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:41.380
The movie opens innocently enough, with our
three leads, Mike, Nick, and Steven, celebrating

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.740
at a wedding and joyously preparing for war.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.080
They ignore the grim warning from a shaken
Green Beret, and when they're finally tossed

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.660
into the jungle, they wind up smack dab in
one of the most horrific movie scenes of all

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.440
time: the Russian roulette sequence.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.560
Captured by the Viet Cong, the friends are
forced to play the suicidal game for the amusement

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:11.740
of their guards, and the acting here is so
intense that it feels like a genuine snuff

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:12.240
film.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:18.660
All David Lynch movies feel a little dreamlike,
but Inland Empire is pure subconscious surrealism,

00:01:18.679 --> 00:01:21.829
a cinematic fugue state that lasts over three
hours.

00:01:21.829 --> 00:01:24.600
It's like you've stumbled straight into Lynch's
worst nightmares.

00:01:24.789 --> 00:01:29.400
The movie is an impenetrably slow descent
into a world of red lights, ambient noises,

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.460
and digital camerawork.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.060
And while you can always appreciate Lynch's
avant garde genius, Inland Empire provides

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.800
more questions than answers.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.720
"They're a group that performs in traveling
shows.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:41.800
In the Baltic Region."

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.920
"What's that got to do with you?"

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.540
For some fans, this might sound like an awesome
experience, but for most moviegoers, Inland

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.060
Empire feels like the world's worst acid trip.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:56.080
It's definitely worth watching once, but when
it's over, you might be a too overwhelmed

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.200
to give it another shot.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:01.979
In The Killing of a Sacred Deer, Colin Farrell
plays a heart surgeon named Steven Murphy

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.000
whose fondness for the bottle contributed
to the death of a patient.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.660
Steven refuses to admit any wrongdoing, and
that's just not going to sit with the patient's

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:12.560
son, an unusual teen by the name of Martin
Lang.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:16.920
"Your son told me that you've got lots of
hair under your arms, three times more than

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.590
I do, and that you've got a very hairy back
and a very hairy belly."

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:26.180
There's something off about Martin, and that's
before he reveals his godlike power to enact

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.100
revenge on Steven's entire family.

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:32.200
As part of his revenge scheme, Martin tells
Steven all his family members are going to

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.780
die of a mysterious illness.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.680
They'll become paralyzed, and then they'll
refuse to eat.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.800
And after they start bleeding from their eyes,
they'll die.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:43.760
The only way Steven can stop this plague is
by killing a member of his family.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.040
The movie gets even darker when the family
turns on each other, arguing why they shouldn't

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:48.860
be the one to die.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:53.600
The desperation, the betrayal, the blood,
it's all so cruel, and it culminates in one

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.040
of the most disturbing climaxes ever filmed.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:00.500
Horrific in ways that no slasher film could
ever achieve, The Killing of a Sacred Deer

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.210
is a powerful film that you won't watch more
than once.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:07.400
Instead, you'll want to put a curse on whoever
recommended the film to you in the first place.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:13.120
"It's the only thing I can think of that's
close to justice."

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:19.200
Released in 2011, Kill List follows Jay, a
soldier-turned-assassin who's fallen on hard

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:19.700
times.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.840
He's got money problems, relationship troubles,
and some serious PTSD.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.880
But things start looking up when he gets a
gig to pick off three easy targets.

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:31.770
However, whenever he shows up to put a cap
in his victims, they start thanking him for

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.580
the privilege of dying by his hand.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:38.140
It's more than a little unsettling, and soon,
Jay realizes he's in the center of an occult

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:42.060
conspiracy that demands a lot of blood and
some really big sacrifices.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.500
Kill List is an all-out assault on the senses.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:48.920
Not only is it one of the most suspenseful
movies ever made, but it's filled with disturbing

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:49.520
sequences.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:54.000
The final showdown with a group of naked pagans
is pure nightmare fuel, but it's the final

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.140
few minutes that will leave you reeling.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:03:57.980
Arachnophobes, beware.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:01.680
If eight-legged creatures give you the willies,
then you might want to stay far away from

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.180
Enemy.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.840
Directed by Denis Villeneuve, this eerie thriller
is full of spider imagery.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.800
Shot in a sickly yellow hue, Enemy stars Jake
Gyllenhaal as a college professor who's made

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.180
an unsettling discovery.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:17.579
After renting a particular film, he spots
an actor who looks exactly like him.

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:21.509
Eventually, the two doppelgängers collide,
and let's just say they don't become best

00:04:21.509 --> 00:04:22.140
of friends.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:27.000
Actor-Gyllenhaal is a grim and violent man
and pulls depressed and weary Professor-Gyllenhaal

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.160
deeper and deeper into his web of darkness.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.620
Playing two roles, Gyllenhaal makes your skin
crawl, with his characters engaging in all

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.260
sorts of unsavory activities.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.460
Enemy is a film that's likely to make you
queasy and uneasy, and that's even before

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.740
you get to the absolutely horrifying ending
scene.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:48.840
"Ah, never know how your day's going to turn
out."

00:04:50.069 --> 00:04:55.139
Based on a tragic true event, Fruitvale Station
tells the story of Oscar Grant, a 22-year-old

00:04:55.139 --> 00:04:59.449
man who was killed by a Bay Area Rapid Transit
officer in 2009.

00:04:59.449 --> 00:05:02.660
We watch Oscar bonding with his daughter and
connecting with strangers.

00:05:02.820 --> 00:05:04.760
We see him smile and laugh, full of life.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:09.059
Sure, he's got some issues, but he's a sincere
guy trying to make things better.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.720
And what hurts is that we know he'll never
get that chance.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.040
Director Ryan Coogler does an excellent job
of showing Oscar as a living, breathing human,

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.320
not just a statistic.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.090
He loves, feels pain, makes mistakes, and
affects so many people.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:24.860
But all his chances for a brighter future
are brought to a bloody halt when he's shot

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.880
in the back for absolutely no reason.

00:05:27.069 --> 00:05:29.780
He leaves behind a child, a girlfriend, and
a mother.

00:05:29.789 --> 00:05:34.029
A human being bleeds to death on New Year's
Day, and as Fruitvale Station comes to an

00:05:34.029 --> 00:05:37.920
end, we're not just depressed, we're mourning
a life that was taken far too soon.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:42.960
In Manchester by the Sea, Casey Affleck plays
Lee Chandler, a handyman who's cut himself

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:43.760
off from the world.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:47.200
The only time he interacts with people is
when he's picking fights at the bar.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:51.280
However, Lee is forced out of hiding when
is brother dies from cardiac arrest.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:55.740
Naturally, Lee has to return to his hometown
to arrange the funeral and care for his nephew

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:56.240
Patrick.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:06:00.620
Eventually, we discover why Lee hates his
hometown and why he's a depressed, angry shell

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:01.180
of a man.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:05.520
One evening, after a night of drinking, Lee
accidentally started a fire that killed his

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:06.020
two kids.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:10.360
Unable to deal with the pain, Lee divorced
his wife and has done his best to disappear.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:14.319
For a moment, it seems like the bond he's
forming with his nephew might save him from

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.520
his past, but this isn't a Hallmark movie.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.760
In the last act, Lee admits the truth to Patrick.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:21.580
"I can't beat it.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:24.200
I'm sorry."

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:29.500
As much as he cares for his nephew, he can't
overcome his depression and guilt.

00:06:29.509 --> 00:06:33.889
There are no easy solutions or feel-good endings
here, and while Manchester by the Sea is a

00:06:33.889 --> 00:06:38.210
beautiful film, wallowing in all that misery
a second time sounds like the most painful

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.900
two hours you could ever spend.

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:45.000
Directed by Denis Villeneuve, Blade Runner
2049 is one of the most gorgeous movies ever

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:45.500
made.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:50.539
A worthy follow-up to the 1982 original, this
stunning sequel nabbed cinematographer Richard

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.840
Deakins the Oscar award he's always deserved.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:58.479
From its barren desert wastelands to its neon
holograms, 2049 is a visually rich world of

00:06:58.479 --> 00:07:03.280
replicants and artificial intelligence, all
beautifully bathed in smog and city lights.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:06.260
However, it's not exactly what you'd call
a fast-paced film.

00:07:06.529 --> 00:07:08.860
In fact, you might even call it a slog.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:13.169
The movie follows Ryan Gosling as K, a blade
runner who stumbles across a mystery that

00:07:13.169 --> 00:07:15.200
might revolutionize the entire world.

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:19.879
Crazier still, he might be at the center of
a vast conspiracy, and during his quest for

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:23.420
the truth, he meets the original blade runner
himself, Rick Deckard.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:27.860
But while K does indeed solve the mystery,
the film takes its sweet time in getting to

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:28.580
the answers.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:34.759
While Blade Runner 2049 is a fantastic work
of science fiction, it runs almost three hours

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.540
long, and even thinking about rewatching it
might be enough to make you a little sleepy.

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.719
After winding up in the world's scariest club,
the members of a punk rock band stumble across

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.820
a particularly nasty murder scene.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:49.700
Knowing the alt-right owners aren't going
to let them walk away, the band members lock

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:52.180
themselves in the titular room and prepare
for war.

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:56.330
But jiu-jitsu will only get you so far when
your opponents are walking around with pistols

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:57.100
and pit bulls.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:08:02.089
With our heroes completely outmatched, Green
Room quickly devolves into a gore-soaked nightmare

00:08:02.089 --> 00:08:04.810
of ripped-out throats and nearly-severed limbs.

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:08.540
Unlike a lot of other horror films, the deaths
in Green Room aren't at all fun.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:13.330
These kids are screaming in genuine pain as
they're mangled by dogs and hacked by machetes.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:17.740
Green Room is fantastic, but at its core,
the movie is as mean and nihilistic as cinema

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:18.240
gets.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:22.320
And while the rockers eventually take their
revenge, so much blood gets splattered on

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.860
the walls by the end that it should probably
be renamed Red Room.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:31.840
A passion project for Martin Scorsese, Silence
features no gangsters, no dirty cops, and

00:08:31.849 --> 00:08:33.630
no taxi-driving assassins.

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:38.601
Instead, the story follows two Jesuit priests,
Father Rodrigues and Father Garupe, as they

00:08:38.601 --> 00:08:41.560
head to Japan to find a missing priest, Father
Ferreira.

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:45.900
Steadfast in his faith, Rodrigues is tested
when he falls into the hands of a ruthless

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:46.860
Japanese governor.

00:08:47.070 --> 00:08:51.740
Practicing Christianity in Japan was punishable
by death in the 17th century, but the governor

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.810
doesn't just want to murder this priest.

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:56.950
He wants to break his spirit and make him
renounce his beliefs.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:09:03.040
"Think of the suffering you have inflicted
on these people, just because of your selfish

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:04.500
dream of a Christian Japan."

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:09.320
On top of the physical torment, Father Rodrigues
is in constant spiritual pain.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:12.400
Should he recant and damn his soul to save
the lives of others?

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.980
And in the midst of all this pain, why is
God so silent?

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:20.660
Whether you're a believer or an atheist, Silence
is a painful reminder that faith is never

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:24.520
easy, and the silence of the universe is the
most painful torture of all.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.360
"We have our own religion, Padre.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.400
A pity you did not know this yet."

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.330
"No, no, we just think a different way."

